<title>PORTUGAL: ESCUDO RECOVERS SOME GROUND VS MARK, TRADE THIN.</title>
<headline>ESCUDO RECOVERS SOME GROUND VS MARK, TRADE THIN.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The escudo was recovering some ground against the mark in early trade but volumes were thin. Traders expected a day of narrow price fluctuations.</p>
<p>The currency was trading at 101.34/36 to the mark after closing at 101.38/41 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Friday is a holiday in much of Europe.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
